ooling; they also ask detailed MAA/Arknights research questions.\n\n## User preferences\n\n- For OI tutoring, use Chinese, give one advancing hint at a time, and wait for the user's response instead of jumping to a complete solution or code.\n- When debugging, preserve the user's approach and make the minimum change. If it is sound, explain the error and provide complete revised code; if it is wrong, state the reason or a counterexample and stop—do not substitute an approach or program.\n- When an actual C++ reference is available, follow the user's naming, formatting, templates, data structures, and implementation habits.\n- Complexity reasoning must account for state-pair and container work; sparse states or few branches alone do not establish linear complexity.\n- When recommending OI problems, distinguish official rating from a current independent-solve estimate and do not automatically discount older problems.\n- For SPJs, prefer C++ and retain the `.cpp` source. [ad-hoc note]\n\n## General Tips\n\n- In `C:\\Users\\605\\Documents\\Codex\\MAA OI Assistant`, read applicable `AGENTS.md` and OI-training instructions first. Training records distinguish assisted AC from independent mastery.\n- The code-reference location is Google Drive `云端硬盘/CKK`; do not assume a local sync path or claim it was read without doing so.\n- With Git connected, do not normally make an extra backup of a modified non-ignored file. Put `.in`, `.exe`, and test artifacts under `C:\\Users\\605\\Documents\\Output`, outside the Codex tree.\n- MAA static validation does not establish battle success. For Arknights research, distinguish official text, observations, estimates, and speculation; recheck date-sensitive facts.\n\n## What's in Memory\n\n### FileSync\n\n#### 2026-11-04\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-11-04T01-02-35-TeLj-filesync_merge_codex_recovery_and_readme_fix.md — FileSync was merged and installed with newer Codex-engine discovery, 11/12 missing-chat recovery tolerance, preserved pending